course: dictionary
lesson: 12973
title: Breathing out: exhale
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Exhale means to breathe out. When you inhale, you breathe air in. When you exhale, you push it back out. «Take a deep breath, then exhale slowly through your mouth.»
explain: The word can also mean sending out air, smoke or gas. «The old chimney exhaled grey smoke into the sky.» The smoke is leaving the chimney, just as breath leaves your mouth.
explain: Look for clues in the words around exhale. Slowly, breath and mouth all point to breathing out. Check by swapping in breathe out: «Breathe out slowly through your mouth» still makes sense, so exhale means breathe out.
fact: Exhale means to breathe out.
fact: Inhale is the opposite: it means to breathe in.
fact: In science, we inhale oxygen and exhale carbon dioxide.
fact: In yoga and PE, «exhale slowly» can help you calm down.
fact: «Exhaled breath» can look like a little cloud on a cold day.
exercise: «Breathe in through your nose, then exhale slowly.» What does exhale mean? | Sneeze loudly | Breathe in | Hold your breath for ages | *Breathe out
exercise: «The old chimney exhaled grey smoke into the sky.» What did the chimney do? | Swallowed the smoke | Cleaned the sky | *Sent out smoke | Painted the sky grey
exercise: In yoga we inhale and exhale. Which word is the opposite of exhale? | Relax | *Inhale | Sneeze | Cough
test: «After running, she stood still and exhaled.» What does exhaled mean? | *Breathed out | Shouted for help | Drank some water | Ran faster
test: Which phrase from science lessons means taking air in and letting it out? | Lungs and heart | Exhale slowly | Hot and cold | *Inhale and exhale
exam: «The tired dog exhaled and lay down by the fire.» Which word has the same meaning as exhaled? | *Breathed out | Barked | Jumped up | Yawned loudly
